From b3faf029dfb1886048af7f76e21c36307b7aae82 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Golle <daniel@makrotopia.org>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 16:16:09 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] [WPE] Let the web process allocate from dma-heaps for an
 external CDM

https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=328385

Reviewed by NOBODY (OOPS!).

The external CDM video decoder puts its pictures into buffers it
allocates from the dma-heap the video sink names, and the GL video sink
tries the heaps to find one EGL imports from. Both run in the web
process, so wherever the CDM blob is bound into the sandbox, bind
/dev/dma_heap as well. This lets the web process allocate system-heap
and physically contiguous memory directly, which is why it comes only
with the external CDM.

* Source/WebKit/UIProcess/Launcher/glib/BubblewrapLauncher.cpp:
(WebKit::bindExternalCDM):

Signed-off-by: Daniel Golle <daniel@makrotopia.org>
---
 Source/WebKit/UIProcess/Launcher/glib/BubblewrapLauncher.cpp | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

--- a/Source/WebKit/UIProcess/Launcher/glib/BubblewrapLauncher.cpp
+++ b/Source/WebKit/UIProcess/Launcher/glib/BubblewrapLauncher.cpp
@@ -478,6 +478,9 @@ static void bindExternalCDM(Vector<CStri
         return;
     bindIfExists(args, cdmPath);
 
+    // The video the CDM decodes goes into buffers from the dma-heap the video sink can import from.
+    args.appendList({ "--dev-bind-try", "/dev/dma_heap", "/dev/dma_heap" });
+
     // An optional preload (e.g. an ifunc resolver) is injected into the web
     // process only, so a glibc CDM blob loads under a libc without ifunc.
     const char* cdmPreload = g_getenv("WPE_WIDEVINE_CDM_PRELOAD");
